  {
   "id": "t1039",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 678,
   "y": 1500,
   "width": 382.8,
   "height": 135.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a0039",
   "seed": 17273,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 33507,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785400000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "1. 20 slugs already carry route + Rigor level. a merge is\n   cross-cutting and owes the standing grep sweep.\n2. retrofit is FORBIDDEN by standing rule - so how does an\n   existing slug acquire a type? forward-only leaves 20\n   items typeless, and the derivation above cannot run\n   backwards without inventing intent.\n3. G6 security has no home in Kerd AT ALL. the hard stop\n   'no production exposure without G6' is currently\n   inexpressible - not failing, inexpressible.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "1. 20 slugs already carry route + Rigor level. a merge is\n   cross-cutting and owes the standing grep sweep.\n2. retrofit is FORBIDDEN by standing rule - so how does an\n   existing slug acquire a type? forward-only leaves 20\n   items typeless, and the derivation above cannot run\n   backwards without inventing intent.\n3. G6 security has no home in Kerd AT ALL. the hard stop\n   'no production exposure without G6' is currently\n   inexpressible - not failing, inexpressible.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t1040",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": 1436,
   "width": 165.0,
   "height": 90.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e03131",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
